# mana-on-turn over its range: Bot1 wears seven, one for each mana it may add and turns 1 to 4 - {W} and {G} on its first
# turn, {U} and {C} on its second, {B} and {C}{C} on its third, {R} on its fourth. Each "at the beginning of your
# precombat main phase, if it's your Nth turn, add ..." triggers there and uses the stack (CR 605.1b: no mana ability), so
# both of a turn's are passed through before the pool holds both, and the pool empties as the phase ends (CR 500.4). No
# trigger on Bot2's turns, on the postcombat main phase (CR 505.1a), or on Bot1's fifth turn.

